[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Be3 Blunder"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pawn-grab"]
[Themes "b2-pawn,counting"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "5...Qb6"]
[Start "advance-qb6 5...Qb6"]

6. Be3 $2 { Looks natural, guarding d4, but the bishop was the only defender of b2. Black's queen now has a free pawn and a strong attack. } 6... Qxb2 $1 { The queen takes b2 and now attacks the rook on a1 as well. White cannot trap it, and Black is a pawn up with a strong attack. } *
